.TH ADMIN 1 "2026" "spicule" "spicule User Commands"
.SH NAME
admin \- create an SCCS file
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B admin
\fB\-i\fR[\fIname\fR]
[\fB\-t\fIname\fR]
[\fB\-y\fR[\fIcomment\fR]]
.I newfile
.br
.B admin
.B \-n
[\fB\-t\fIname\fR]
[\fB\-y\fR[\fIcomment\fR]]
.I newfile
.RI [ newfile ]\ .\|.\|.
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B admin
creates a new SCCS history file for each
.I newfile
operand, with a single initial delta whose SCCS ID (SID) is
.BR 1.1 .
.PP
This implementation only creates new
.I s.
files; it does not modify the control parameters of an existing one.
Given an operand that already exists, or neither
.B \-i
nor
.B \-n
at all,
.B admin
refuses with a diagnostic rather than doing nothing silently.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-i\fR[\fIname\fR]
Take the initial file content from
.IR name .
If
.I name
is omitted, the content is read from standard input instead. Exactly
one
.I newfile
operand may be given with
.BR \-i .
.TP
.B \-n
Create the SCCS file with control information but no initial file
content (an empty first delta). One or more
.I newfile
operands may be given with
.BR \-n .
.TP
\fB\-t\fIname\fR
Take descriptive text for the SCCS file from
.IR name .
Unlike the base standard,
.I name
is required whenever
.B \-t
is given; a bare
.B \-t
with no attached name is refused.
.TP
\fB\-y\fR[\fIcomment\fR]
Use
.I comment
as the comment recorded for the initial delta. If
.B \-y
is given with no attached text, the comment is empty. If
.B \-y
is omitted entirely, a comment of the form \(dqdate and time created
.I YY/MM/DD HH:MM:SS
by
.I user\(dq
is synthesized instead.
.PP
Every other option (including
.BR \-a ,
.BR \-d ,
.BR \-e ,
.BR \-f ,
.BR \-m ,
.BR \-r ,
.BR \-h ,
and
.BR \-z ,
all of which a real
.B admin
uses to modify or audit an
.I already-existing
SCCS file) is refused with a diagnostic; none of them is implemented.
Every SCCS file this implementation creates therefore always has the
fixed initial SID
.BR 1.1 .
.SH OPERANDS
.TP
.I newfile
The pathname of an SCCS file to create. Its basename must begin with
the literal two characters \(dqs.\(dq; an operand that does not is
refused with a diagnostic, and processing continues with the next
operand.
.SH APPLICATION USAGE
A newly created SCCS file is given read-only permission mode
(0444), matching real SCCS behavior.
.PP
Since this implementation has no counterpart for
.BR delta (1)
(committing a second delta to an existing file), every SCCS file it
can produce has exactly one delta; the user-list and flags sections a
real, actively-maintained SCCS file uses are written but always
empty.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Every
.I newfile
operand was processed successfully.
.TP
.B 1
An operand was skipped (already existed, wrong basename, an
unimplemented option was given, or an I/O error occurred); processing
continues with any remaining operands.
.TP
.B 2
A usage error: no operand was given, or
.B \-i
was combined with more than one
.I newfile
operand.
.SH EXAMPLES
Create
.B s.hello.c
from an existing file, with a comment:
.nf
admin \-ihello.c \-y"initial checkin" s.hello.c
.fi
.PP
Create an empty SCCS file, then check in the same content later
retrieves correctly:
.nf
admin \-n s.empty
get \-p s.empty
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR get (1)
